## 6. Common Problems and Solutions

| Problem | Expected | Possible issue | Solution |
|---|---|---|---|
| No internet | Successful ping | Network issue | `ipconfig /all`; check network mode |
| No IP address | Valid IP | `169.254.x.x` | `ipconfig /release`; `ipconfig /renew` |
| Adapter disabled | Status Up | Disabled adapter | `Get-NetAdapter`; `Enable-NetAdapter -Name "Ethernet"` |
| DNS problem | Domain resolves | IP works, domain fails | `nslookup google.com` |
| Wrong network mode | Internet connection | Host-only mode | Change to NAT |
| Disk not visible | Disk appears | Missing disk/partition | `Get-Disk`, `Get-Partition`, `Get-Volume` |
| Disk full | Free space | Low storage | `Get-Volume` / `df -h` |
| Ubuntu no internet | Successful ping | Network configuration | `ip addr`, `ip route` |
| VM too slow | Normal performance | Low RAM / CPU | `free -h`, `top` |
| VM won't start | VM boots | Insufficient resources | Check RAM, CPU, disk |
| DHCP service stopped | Running | Stopped | `Get-Service -Name Dhcp` |

**Important:** Do not format or initialize a disk before confirming that it is the correct disk. Formatting can erase data.

